<p style="text-align: center;">Bainbridge Point. 5x7, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This one took a lot of experimentation. I had to keep painting and destroying the forms over and over again until I got what I was looking for. I've always been very careful about mixing my paint and keeping everything super tidy, so it's a big change to put all that discipline to one side and be willing to risk a muddy mess.</p>